Z||000009||FieroRacer||11-16-2001||11:04 PM||||Very rough estimates.  3.1L With Low Performance Fully Ported Heads and 1.8/1.52" Valves.  9.1:1 Compression, 850cfm Airflow, Large Tube Headers with Mufflers, Stage Two ARI Camshaft.<P>Desktop Dyno puts you at the following:<BR>253hp@6500<BR>250ft-lbs@4000<P>At the engine.<P>I can't be very accurate at all though without better specs.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Shaun41178||11-16-2001||11:31 PM||||Fieroracer:  Come on man 850 cfm airflow?  That is more then some big v8's!!!  No wonder it makes 253 hp.  3.1 probably flows more like 350 cfm or in that area.  Drop that cfm down to where you will have about 160 hp from the program and that is roughly what a 3.1 will flow cfm wise.<P>Hey Turkey.  You say you have larger valves.  mind explaining which valves you had put in?  Also what are the diameters of the int and exh valves?<P>Also 2.5 inch headers?  ARe you talking abuot the primary headers like right off the heads?  If so then those headers are way too big!!  350's use like 1-7/8 as headers and even those lose low end torque but do gain some high end.  Most go with 1-5/8 with a v8 like a 350.  I am guessing you mean cat-back though?<P>If I had to guess without knowing your cam specs and everything else, I would guess your hp range to be in the 165-170 range at the crank which will be around 135 or so at the wheels.<P>Most stock 2.8 Fieros dyno around 115 at the wheels<P>It is going to take an awefull lot to get a 3.1 over 200 hp.  Gm had a all aluminum 3.4 in the 90 Beretta Pace car with ported aluminum heads and a custom intake with a huge lift cam(.560 in mechanical, solid lifters) it made about 245 hp at the crank at a whopping 6800 rpm.  Just an FYI||||reg||5
Z||000011||88formula||11-17-2001||01:57 PM||||I'm guessing you have the Lunati 53505 camshaft with 268 degrees of duration. If so than your car would make around 184 horsepower @ 5500 RPM and 210-ft. lbs. of torque @ 4000 RPM at the best. <P>I used Dyno2000 and 350 cfm for the throttle body.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 11-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||FieroRacer||11-17-2001||07:14 PM||||OK, I've revised my settings:<P>3.1L Block<BR>Low Performance Fully Ported Heads (1.8/1.52 Valves)<BR>9.1:1 CR<BR>350 cfm SEFI<BR>HP Manifolds and Exhaust (thinking he went with 2.5" exhaust)<BR>High Performance Street Cam<P>198hp@6000<BR>195ft-lbs@4500<P>I don't have Lunati's Cam Specs though||||reg||1
